		<h1>Privacy Notice for California Residents</h1>
		<p class="updated">Effective Date: 03/2026</p>

		<h2>Introduction</h2>
		<p>This Privacy Notice for California Residents (“Notice”) describes the privacy practices of BG Clear, LLC and its affiliates and subsidiaries (collectively, “BG Clear,” “we,” “our,” or “us”) in connection with the personal information we collect about California residents and households (“you” or “Consumers”). This Notice applies to all the personal information that BG Clear collects when Consumers interact with us, such as when visiting our websites, using or purchasing our products or services, contacting customer service and when interacting with us as a business customer, supplier, or business partner (collectively, the “Services”). This Notice supplements our general Privacy Statement, except as noted in the rights section below.</p>

		<h2>Overview</h2>
		<p>We believe in helping you understand our privacy practices concerning your information. Driven by that goal, we have prepared this brief overview of key points about why and how we process your information:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>What personal information do we collect?</strong> We collect the following categories of personal information: identifiers, inferences, customer records, protected characteristics, internet or other electronic network activity information, geolocation data, biometric information, professional and employment information, sensory details, and sensitive personal information. You can find more details on those categories in the section below.</li>
			<li><strong>How do you use my information?</strong> We use your information to communicate with you, conduct our business (such as delivering and improving the Services), and comply with our legal obligations. A more detailed explanation is below.</li>
			<li><strong>Do you sell or share my information?</strong> We “sell” or “share” your information, as those terms are defined under California’s privacy law, in limited circumstances. Specifically, when you opt-in to targeting cookies, we allow our partners to collect (using cookies) limited personal information in order to provide you more relevant advertising.</li>
			<li><strong>How long do you keep my information?</strong> We retain your information for the period specified in our retention policy, unless legally or contractually required to keep it longer.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Collection and Use of Information</h2>
		<p>We collect information that identifies, relates to, describes, references, is reasonably capable of being associated with, or could reasonably be linked, directly or indirectly, with Consumers ("personal information"). Specifically, in the last 12 months, BG Clear collected the following categories of personal information from Consumers:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Identifiers.</strong> This includes information such as your name, income level, contact details, government identification, and demographic details.</li>
			<li><strong>Inferences.</strong> We may draw inferences about your preferences or other characteristics using information we have about you.</li>
			<li><strong>Customer Records.</strong> This includes information such as your name, contact details, transaction or purchase history, government identification, and payment information.</li>
			<li><strong>Protected Characteristics.</strong> This includes information such as your age and criminal background history.</li>
			<li><strong>Internet or Other Electronic Network Activity Information.</strong> This includes information about your use of our IT services and networks, such as your browsing history on company devices.</li>
			<li><strong>Geolocation Data.</strong> We may collect your location.</li>
			<li><strong>Professional and Employment Information.</strong> This includes information such as your employer, work history, and professional qualifications.</li>
			<li><strong>Sensory Details.</strong> This includes information such as pictures, video, and oral recordings of you.</li>
			<li><strong>Sensitive Personal Information.</strong> This includes information such as your health information, login credentials, government identification, payment information, and precise geolocation.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We may collect personal information about you from a variety of sources, including:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>From You:</strong> We collect information that you submit to us. For example, when you use the Services, register to receive information, products or services available through the Services or interact with us in other ways, we will collect any information you voluntarily provide, and we may also request optional information to support your use of the Services. We also collect any information that you voluntarily enter into any postings, comments, or forums within the Services. If you send an e-mail to us, we will collect your e-mail address and the full content of your e-mail, including attached files and other information you choose to provide to us.</li>
			<li><strong>From Your Devices:</strong> When you use our Services, we may collect information about the devices you use to access the Services, including hardware model, operating system and version, IP address and other unique device identifiers, mobile network information, and information about the device’s interaction with our Services. We also collect information about how you use our Services, including your access times, browser types, and language. This type of data enables us to understand how often individuals use parts of the Services so we can analyze and improve them. To collect this information, we use cookies and web beacons, and other similar technologies.</li>
			<li><strong>Social Media Networks and Other Third Parties:</strong> We may obtain information about you or your use of the Services from third parties and sources, such as our vendors, like web hosting providers, analytics providers, or advertisers. You may give us permission to access your information from services offered by third parties, including social media networks. The information we obtain from third party services depends on your account/privacy settings with those third parties and the third parties’ privacy policies, so please check those policies and adjust your settings to meet your preferences.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>BG Clear may process the personal information we collect for one or more of the following purposes:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>To deliver products and services.</li>
			<li>To activate or register certain products and services or enhance functionality.</li>
			<li>To send information about BG Clear products and services.</li>
